   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Project Viv&#xe1; Boipeba, Small Island, Broad Horizons</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project &#x201c;Viv&#xe1; Ilha Boipeba: Small Island, Broad Horizons&#x201d; aiming to promote sustainable development on the island of Boipeba, Bahia, in the Northeast region of Brazil and addresses the urgent need for education and professional skills development in a marginalized Afro-Brazilian/Indigenous community affected by unregulated tourism and environmental degradation. The target group is of approximately 800 people including women of all ages and young people from three of the main communities on the island.</narrative>
  </description>
